rt in the  scholarship and grant  process and we want to remind everybody  by the way they're always lower-cost  options you don't have to go for the  most expensive school it's what you make  of that college experience so often  investing also obviously so big for  people and you say play your own game  what does that mean well look we always  hear about these rules of thumb around  investment advice that's kind of bunk  because you've really got to know  yourself as an investor and I have  pretty much like five outline tips that  people should keep in mind first is you  should not be investing unless you've  covered what I call the big three  meaning you've got to pay down your  outstanding debt you've got to have the  emergency reserve fund you've got to be  using your retirement account you've got  to max it to the best of your ability  now from there you want to create a  financial plan then you comes your asset  allocation I happen to like index funds  they're cheap so that's good we want you  to stick to the plan but you want to  revisit that plan when something goes on  in your life so it could be a birth a  death a divorce a marriage and we also  want you to just get in the habit of  revisiting it every few years there was  a fabulous party for you this past week  can we say we were very excited for you  in your new book but the highlight of  the party is was meeting your mom and  for her as well Susan I mean Anthony and  Susan what a star she was crushing on it  I was so happy to see her and we wish  you all the best with the book thank you  Jill thank you very much
 

